---
import artistPortrait from '../assets/artist-portrait.jpg';
import ArtworkImage from '../components/ArtworkImage.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSortedArtworks } from '../lib/artworks';

const artworks = await getSortedArtworks();
const processArtwork = artworks.find((artwork) => artwork.data.images.some((image) => image.type === 'process'));
const processImage = processArtwork?.data.images.find((image) => image.type === 'process');
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About the artist and material practice behind Endeavor Art Studio.">
  <header class="page-heading page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About / Artist and practice</p>
    <h1>Material leads.<br />The work follows.</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="bio page-shell" aria-labelledby="bio-title">
    <figure>
      <ArtworkImage
        src={artistPortrait}
        alt="Illustrated portrait of Chelsea in a pink beret riding an electric scooter past flames"
        sizes="(min-width: 768px) 42vw, 100vw"
        loading="eager"
      />
      <figcaption>Chelsea, artist</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <h2 id="bio-title" class="section-label">Biography</h2>
      <p class="large-copy">Chelsea</p>
      <p>Chelsea is a mixed-media artist whose work is rooted in texture, intention, and the deeply held belief that sometimes the best thing you can do to a perfectly good bottle is smash it and turn the remains into something better. Her process is surprisingly deliberate: each piece is carefully planned, composed, and refined until the materials land exactly where she wants them. Much like Chelsea herself, the finished work tends to be bold, direct, and considerably more approachable once you spend a little time with it.</p>
      <p>Outside the studio, Chelsea maintains a rigorous creative practice consisting of working out, consuming gin and tonics, making her celebrated Ghetto Pasta, and causing mayhem on her local neighborhood streets aboard an electric scooter with absolutely no indication that she considers this unusual behavior for an adult. Scooting is not merely transportation; it is a lifestyle. A calling. Possibly a mobility-based personality disorder. When she is not scooting, she can occasionally be found appreciating the finer performing arts, particularly Yung Gravy and the timeless cultural institution of little-person wrestling.</p>
      <p>Chelsea is also an accomplished Glizzy Gobbler, a title earned not through self-promotion but through years of consistent performance in the highly competitive field of putting away hot dogs. She approaches the glizzy with the same focus and commitment she brings to her artwork: confidently, efficiently, and without unnecessary discussion. Her other culinary achievements include fajitas and the aforementioned Ghetto Pasta, which remains both a meal and an important reminder that branding can overcome almost anything.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="statement section page-shell" aria-labelledby="statement-title">
    <div>
      <h2 id="statement-title" class="section-label">Artist statement</h2>
      <span class="draft-note">Draft for artist review</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="large-copy">I am drawn to materials that already carry evidence of use, breakage, pressure, and change.</p>
      <div class="statement-columns">
        <p>Temporary first-person copy: The work develops through handling. Glass, ceramic, resin, found objects, and built-up surfaces are tested against one another until their familiar purpose gives way to a new relationship.</p>
        <p>Temporary first-person copy: Fragments are not treated as damage to hide. Their edges, gaps, and points of contact become part of the composition. Experimentation remains visible in the finished piece.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
    {processImage && (
      <div class="process-image">
        <ArtworkImage
          src={processImage.src}
          alt={processImage.alt}
          caption="Process photograph"
          sizes="(min-width: 768px) 62vw, 100vw"
          lightbox
          gallery="artist-process"
        />
      </div>
    )}
    <div class="process-copy">
      <h2 id="process-title" class="section-label">Artistic process</h2>
      <span class="draft-note">Draft for artist review</span>
      <h3>Collect. Test. Break. Reassemble.</h3>
      <p>Materials may suggest the initial direction, but the outcome is not fixed in advance. Construction, removal, and revision continue until the surface and structure feel resolved.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-heading {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 12rem);
  }

  .page-heading h1 {
    max-width: 85rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0 auto;
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 10rem);
  }

  .bio {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(20rem, 1.15fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 10rem);
    align-items: center;
    padding-bottom: var(--section-space);
  }

  .bio figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bio figcaption {
    padding-top: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .bio > div > p:not(.large-copy) {
    max-width: 38rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
  }

  .bio > div > p.large-copy {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .statement {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .statement-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 6rem);
    margin-top: 4rem;
    color: var(--paper-muted);
  }

  .process {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(20rem, 0.8fr);
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--charcoal);
  }

  .process-image :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 90svh;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .process-copy {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 8rem) var(--page-pad);
  }

  .process-copy h3 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 47.99rem) {
    .page-heading h1 {
      margin-left: 0;
    }

    .bio,
    .statement,
    .process {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .bio figure {
      width: calc(100% + var(--page-pad) * 2);
      margin-left: calc(var(--page-pad) * -1);
    }

    .bio figcaption {
      padding-left: var(--page-pad);
    }

    .statement-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .process-copy {
      padding-block: 5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
